  <running_head>GEOGRAPH. LIB. I.</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>Quiq;</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <p><i>Petráque Olenia,&amp; Alisium,intus continet:</i> <note side="left">Alisium.</note></p>
    <p><i>His quidem Amphimacus,Thalpius,Diores,&amp; Polyxenus præerant.:</i></p>
    <p><i>Ætolis autem imperabat Thoas Andræmonis filius,</i> <note side="left">Ætoli.</note></p>
    <p><i>Qui Pleurona habitabant,&amp; Olenum,&amp; Pylenem,</i> <note side="left">Pleron. Olenos. Pyle-ne. Chalcis. Calydon.</note></p>
    <p><i>Chalcidáque maritimam,Calydonáque petrosam.</i></p>
    <p><i>His imperabat flauus Meleager.</i></p>
    <p><i>Nunc autem ipsos quicúnque Pelasgicum Argos habitabant:</i> <note side="left">Thessalia.</note></p>
    <p><i>Quíque Alon, quíque Alopen, quíque Thrachinam incolebant:</i> <note side="left">Alon. Alope. Trachina mons.</note></p>
    <p><i>Quíque tenebant Phthiam,&amp; Hellada,</i> <note side="left">Phthia. Hellai.</note></p>
    <p><i>Myrmidones autem vocabantur, &amp; Hellenes, &amp; Achiui:</i></p>
    <p><i>His erat princeps velox Achilles.</i></p>
    <p><i>Qui autem habitabant Philacen, &amp; Pyrrhasum floridam.</i> <note side="left">Phylace.</note></p>
    <p><i>Cereris nemus,Itonáque matrem ouium,</i> <note side="left">Iton oppid. Antron. Pteleum.</note></p>
    <p><i>Maritimámque Antrona,&amp; Pteleum herbosum:</i></p>
    <p><i>Horum Protesilaus bellicosus dux erat.</i></p>
    <p><i>Qui autem Pheras habitabant apud Boebeiden paludem,</i> <note side="left">Pheræ. Boebis pal.</note></p>
    <p><i>Boebem,&amp; Glaphyras,&amp; bene ædificatam Iolcum:</i> <note side="left">Iolcos. Glaphyras.</note></p>
    <p><i>His imperabat Eumelus Admeti filius.</i></p>
    <p><i>Quivero Methonem, &amp; Thaumaciam habitabant,</i> <note side="left">Methone. Thaumacia. Meliboea.</note></p>
    <p><i>Et Meliboeam tenebant,&amp; Olizonem asperam:</i> <note side="left">Olizone.</note></p>
    <p><i>His Philoctetes præerat.</i></p>
    <p><i>Quíque habitabant Triccem,&amp; Ithonem asperam.</i> <note side="left">Tricce. Ithone.</note></p>
    <p><i>Quíque incolebant Oechaliam ciuitatem Euryti Oechalij:</i> <note side="left">Oechalia.</note></p>
    <p><i>His præerant Æsculapij duo filij.</i></p>
    <p><i>Quíque tenebant Ormenium, quiq; fontem Hyperiam,</i> <note side="left">Hyperias fl.</note></p>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Marginal labels are the place-name keywords in the left margin. Bottom-right word reads "Quiq;" and is printed as a catchword. Some Greek-letter and italic forms are approximate.</notes>
</page>
